$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Pd(Quinox)Cl2-TBHP
Oxidation. In the dark, AgSbF6 (25.8 mg, 0.075 mmol, 0.075 equiv) and
Pd(quinox)Cl2 (11.3 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv) were added to a 25-mL
round bottomed flask with a stir bar. CH2Cl2 (1.7 mL) was charged to the
flask and the mixture was stirred for 10 min, after which time TBHP (1.7
mL, 12 mmol, 12 equiv) was added along with the remaining CH2Cl2 (6.6
mL), turning the mixture from pale yellow to orange. The flask was placed
in an ice bath, and after 10 min the substrate (1.0 mmol, 1 equiv) was
added. The reaction mixture was allowed to slowly warm to room
temperature. Once TLC analysis indicated complete consumption of the
starting material, the reaction was cooled to 0 °C and quenched with a
saturated solution of Na2SO3 (15 mL) to consume excess TBHP. The mixture
was transferred to a separatory funnel and diluted with hexanes (25 mL).
The aqueous layer was extracted with hexanes (3 × 25 mL). The combined
organic phases were washed with H2O (3 × 10 mL) and brine (25 mL) and
then dried over MgSO4. After filtration and concentration under reduced
pressure, the crude material was purified by flash chromatography and the
product containing fractions were combined and concentrated under reduced
pressure. 2-Oxononan-4-yl Acetate (7). The general procedure for the
TBHP-mediated Wacker oxidation was followed using non-1-en-4-yl acetate 6
(197 mg, 1.07 mmol) and purified by flash chromatography eluting with 15%
ethyl acetate in hexanes. Hydroxynonan-2-one (Table 2, entry 1, 9). The
general procedure for the TBHP-mediated Wacker oxidation was followed
using non-1-en-4-ol 8 (142 mg, 1.00 mmol and 152 mg, 1.07 mmol
respectively). The crude mixtures were purified by flash chromatography
eluting with 33% ethyl acetate in hexanes. 4-hydroxynonan-2-one 9 (132
mg, 0.83 mmol and 123 mg, 0.78 mmol respectively) as a colorless oil in
an 81% average yield. The spectral data were in accordance with the
previous report.25
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, regioselective, safety (concentrated solutions of TBHP in
the presence of transition metals can be explosive), Wacker oxidation,
reactant also recovered, optimization study (optimized on catalyst
loading, time and temperature)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalyst-controlled Wacker-type oxidation of homoallylic alcohols in the
absence of protecting groups
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM McCombs, Jessica R.; Michel, Brian W.; Sigman, Matthew S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2011), 76(9), 3609-3613

