$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2 catalyzed Direct
O2 coupled Wacker Oxidation Procedure In a 75 mL schlenk flask equipped
with a stirbar, 3.3 mg Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2 (0.008 mmol, 0.01 equiv.) and
4 mL of a 4:1 (v/v) solution of DMA:H2O were combined. The flask was
placed in an oil bath heated to 70 ˚C and stirred to dissolve catalyst
(ca. 10 minutes), at which time the flask was allowed to cool to room
temperature. A condenser was then attached to the flask and a three-way
joint fitted with a balloon of O2 was installed on the condenser. The
flask was evacuated via house vacuum and refilled with oxygen three times
and the mixture was stirred vigorously for ca. 10 minutes at room
temperature. Using a syringe, 178 μL of dodecene (0.8 mmol, 1 equiv.) was
added at room temperature. Following substrate addition, the reaction
flask was placed into a 70 ˚C oil bath. The reaction mixture was stirred
vigorously under a balloon of O2. After 18 h, the flask was removed from
the oil bath and condenser walls were rinsed with ca. 2 mL Et2O. The
reaction mixture was transferred to a 60 mL sep. funnel and washed twice
with ca. 4 mL of 1N HCl(aq).The aqueous layers were combined and back
extracted three times with ca. 4 mL Et2O. The organic layers were
combined and washed with ca. 5 mL brine. The organic layer was dried over
MgSO4 and filtered. Product was purified from catalyst and remaining
solvent via flash column chromatography using 1-5% Et2O/pentane solvent
gradient. Fractions containing product were collected and solvent removed
in vacuo. Purity was confirmed via 1H-NMR. Table 3 Entry 4
(1-PMBO-1-phenyl-3-butanone). Purified via flash chromatography using 20%
Et2O in pentane to afford product in 80 % yield. Characterization data:
clear oil. clear oil. IR (neat) 2933, 1721, 1612, 1516, 1454, 1357, 1302,
1253, 1173, 1087, 1038, 822, 755, 702, 548 cm-1; 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.27-7.41 (m, 5H), 7.14-7.22 (d, 2H, J=8.8 Hz), 6.82-6.89 (d, 2H,J=8.8
Hz), 4.82-4.88 (dd, 1H, J=4.4, 9.1 Hz) 4.19-4.37 (dd, 2H, J=11.0, 36.1
Hz), 3.8 (s, 3H), 2.97-3.08 (dd, 2H, J=9.1, 15.9 Hz), 2.56-2.65 (dd, 2H,
J=4.3, 15.8 Hz), 2.13 (s, 3H); 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 206.8, 159.4,
141.5, 130.4, 129.8, 128.9, 128.2, 126.9, 114.0, 77.5, 70.6, 55.5, 52.3,
31.2. MS (EI) m/z (M)+ calc 284.14, obsd. 284.05.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Practical Direct O2-Coupled Wacker Oxidation with
Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
