$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The 4-pentenals 3a-h, PdCl2 (10 mol%), and
CuCl2 (10 mol%) were dissolved in aqueous DME (1:9) and stirred under an
oxygen atmosphere for 2-3 h. When the reaction was observed to be
complete, normal aqueous extractive work-up gave the ketoaldehydes 4a-h
in 71-84% yield. Compound 4h. solid, yield 76% Bp/Mp [°C] (Torr): 58-60;
IR [cm-1] (neat/nujol): 2685.0, 1721.0, 1698.0.; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ J (Hz):
2.17 (s, 3 H, -CO-CH3), 2.62 (d, 1 H, J= 11.3 Hz, -CH2-CO-), 3.31 (m, 1
H, -CH-CHO), 3.84 (s, 6 H, 2 × -OCH3), 4.15 (br s, 1 H, -CH2-CO-), 6.64
(s, 1 H, Ar-H), 6.69 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1 H, Ar-H), 6.82 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1
H, Ar-H), 9.63 (s, 1 H, -CHO); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ : 27.6 (CH3-C=O), 43.6
(CH2- C=O), 52.7 (Ar-C-CHO), 55.9, 56.2 (2 × -OCH3), 113.1 (Carom5meta),
114.2 (Carom2ortho), 121.7 (Carom6ortho), 130.7 (Carom1), 147.3
(Carom4para), 148.1 (Carom3meta), 203.8 (-CHO), 206.5 (CH3-C=O);
Microanalysis calcd/found: C: 66.08 65.98; H: 6.83 6.87.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
