$DATUM Tricyclic diketone 21: To a stirred solution of tricyclic keto amide 20
(220.0 mg, 0.550 mmol) in DMF (5.0 mL) and H2O (0.5 mL) were added CuCl
(80.0 mg, 0.810 mmol) and PdCl2 (24.0 mg, 0.140 mmol) at room
temperature. The resulting mixture was bubbled with oxygen for 30 min and
stirred under an oxygen atmosphere at that temperature for 12 h. After
filtration through celite, the residue so obtained was purified by flash
column chromatography with EtOAc/petroleum ether (1:1 - 2:1) to give
tricyclic diketone 21. 21 as a pale yellow sticky oil, yield 180.0 mg,
79%. Rf = 0.29 (silica, EtOAc:petroleum ether 2:1); [α]D25 = -32.1 (c =
0.41 in CHCl3); IR (film): νmax = 3445, 3017, 2951, 2923, 2867, 2854,
1738, 1715, 1708, 1646, 1455, 1405, 1373, 1359, 1337, 1261, 1206, 1168,
1114, 1078, 1064, 1020, 803, 732, 666 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
5.73 (ddd, J = 9.9, 4.7, 2.4 Hz, 1 H), 5.59 (d, J = 9.9 Hz, 1 H), 4.89
(t, J = 6.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.14-4.01 (m, 2 H), 3.93-3.79 (m, 2 H), 3.70 (s, 3
H), 3.20 (s, 3 H), 2.56 (t, J = 6.3 Hz, 1 H), 2.37 (dd, J = 11.3, 4.6 Hz,
1 H), 2.27 (s, 3 H), 1.90-1.68 (m, 3 H), 1.49-1.38 (m, 3 H), 1.15-1.02
(m, 1 H), 0.98 (s, 3 H), 0.94-0.78 (m, 5 H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 212.50, 209.35, 170.23, 168.71, 133.85, 123.72, 60.72, 60.51,
56.38, 55.72, 52.45, 52.15, 47.37, 41.58, 38.39, 36.96, 35.29, 34.72,
32.98, 31.88, 25.19, 22.39, 15.40 ppm; HRMS (m/z): [M + Na]+ calcd for
C23H33NO6Na+ 442.2200; found 442.2205.
