$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Wacker Oxidation of 3; General Procedure In a
solution of substituted, functionalized olefin 3a-h (1 equiv), in aq THF
(THF/H2O, 1:9), were suspended PdCl2 (0.1 equiv) and CuCl2 (0.1 equiv).
This mixture was stirred at r.t. under O2 (TLC control, 6-8 h). The
mixture was diluted with H2O and extracted with Et2O (3 × 20 mL). The
combined Et2O layers were washed with H2O, dried (Na2SO4), concentrated
in vacuo and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
using 98:2 hexane-EtOAc as eluent (Table 3). Compound 5e, yield 79%. Bp
(°C)/Torr): 71-75/0.5. IR (neat/Nujol) (cm-1) 2926, 2717, 1726, 1679,
1626, 1461, 1229, 1107, 1023, 722, 659. 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ, J (Hz) 0.89
(t, J= 6.3, 3 H, CH2CH3), 1.26 [br s, 14 H, (CH2)7], 1.40-1.50 [m, 1 H,
CH3(CH2)7CHA], 1.85- 2.00 [m, 1 H, CH3(CH2)7CHB], 2.40 (s, 3 H, COCH3),
3.50 (t, J= 7.2, 1 H, CH2CHCHO), 5.90 (s, 1 H, C=CHA E to acyl), 6.30 (s,
1 H, C=CHB Z to acyl), 9.62 (s, 1 H, CHO). 13C NMR (CDCl3), δ 14.00,
22.57, 25.40, 27.19, 28.19, 29.18, 29.30, 29.38, 29.41, 31.76, 52.91,
128.23, 145.86, 198.37, 200.63.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM eliminative Wacker oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Eliminative Wacker oxidation: An efficient synthesis of α-alkyl vinyl
methyl ketones
