$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Wacker Oxidation of 3; General Procedure In a
solution of substituted, functionalized olefin 3a-h (1 equiv), in aq THF
(THF/H2O, 1:9), were suspended PdCl2 (0.1 equiv) and CuCl2 (0.1 equiv).
This mixture was stirred at r.t. under O2 (TLC control, 6-8 h). The
mixture was diluted with H2O and extracted with Et2O (3 × 20 mL). The
combined Et2O layers were washed with H2O, dried (Na2SO4), concentrated
in vacuo and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
using 98:2 hexane-EtOAc as eluent (Table 3). Compound 5d, yield 79%. Bp
(°C)/Torr): 72-75/1. IR (neat/Nujol) (cm-1) 3196, 2927, 2719, 1722, 1678,
1626, 1458, 1099, 738, 699. 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ, J (Hz) 0.87 (t, J= 6.3, 3
H, CH2CH3), 1.26 [br s, 10 H, (CH2)5], 1.46-1.53 [m, 1 H, CH3(CH2)5CHA],
1.87- 1.95 (m, 1 H, CH3(CH2)5CHB), 2.39 (s, 3 H, COCH3), 3.49 (t, J= 7.5,
1 H, CHCHO), 5.88 (s, 1 H, C=CHA E to acyl), 6.29 (s, 1 H, C=CHB Z to
acyl), 9.61 (s, 1 H, CHO). 13C NMR (CDCl3), δ 14.00, 22.55, 25.45, 27.23,
28.26, 28.99, 29.38, 31.70, 52.94, 128.20, 145.94, 198.42, 200.68.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM eliminative Wacker oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Eliminative Wacker oxidation: An efficient synthesis of α-alkyl vinyl
methyl ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kulkarni, Mukund G.; Davawala, Saryu I.; Doke, Aniruddha K.; Gaikwad,
Dayaneshwar D.; Doke, Ajit V.
