$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Wacker Oxidation of 3; General Procedure In a
solution of substituted, functionalized olefin 3a-h (1 equiv), in aq THF
(THF/H2O, 1:9), were suspended PdCl2 (0.1 equiv) and CuCl2 (0.1 equiv).
This mixture was stirred at r.t. under O2 (TLC control, 6-8 h). The
mixture was diluted with H2O and extracted with Et2O (3 × 20 mL). The
combined Et2O layers were washed with H2O, dried (Na2SO4), concentrated
in vacuo and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
using 98:2 hexane-EtOAc as eluent (Table 3). Compound 5g, yield 78%. IR
(neat/Nujol) (cm-1) 3029, 2924, 2724, 1722, 1678, 1626, 1454, 1098, 1028,
739, 699. 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ, J (Hz) 0.87, 0.89 (d, J= 6.6, 3 H, CHCH3),
1.10-1.20 (m, 2 H, CH2CHCH2), 1.20-1.55 (m, 5 H, CHCH2CH2), 1.59 (s, 3 H,
HC=CCH3), 1.68 (s, 3 H, HC=CCH3), 1.82-2.02 (m, 2 H, CH2CH=CMe2), 2.40
(s, 3 H, COCH3), 3.45 (t, J= 6, 1 H, CH2CHCHO), 5.00-5.10 (m, 1 H,
CH=CMe2), 5.88 (s, 1 H, C=CHA E to acyl), 6.29 (s, 1 H, C=CHB Z to acyl),
9.60 (s, 1 H, CHO). 13C NMR (CDCl3), δ 17.61, 19.31, 19.45, 25.43, 25.45,
25.48, 25.68, 25.73, 25.90, 32.28, 32.40, 34.38, 34.49, 36.72, 36.88,
53.23, 124.68, 128.19, 128.24, 131.16, 145.95, 146.05, 198.42, 200.65.
