$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The 4-pentenals 3a-h, PdCl2 (10 mol%), and
CuCl2 (10 mol%) were dissolved in aqueous DME (1:9) and stirred under an
oxygen atmosphere for 2-3 h. When the reaction was observed to be
complete, normal aqueous extractive work-up gave the ketoaldehydes 4a-h
in 71-84% yield. Compound 4d. solid, yield 76% Bp/Mp [°C] (Torr): 41-42;
IR [cm-1] (neat/nujol): 2712.1, 1718.1, 1705.6.; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ J (Hz):
1.22 (s, 3 H, -C-CH3), 1.72- 1.85 (m, 2 H, -C-CH2-C-), 2.12 (s, 3 H,
-COCH3), 2.46 (t, 2 H, J = 8.5 Hz, Ar-CH2-), 2.67 (d, 1 H, J = 17.7 Hz,
-CO-CH2-), 2.84 (d, 1 H, J = 17.7 Hz, -COCH2-), 3.77 (s, 3 H, -OCH3),
6.81 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2 H, Ar-H), 7.05 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2 H, Ar-H), 9.58
(s, 1 H, -CHO); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ : 20.5 (-C-CH3), 26.3 (CH3- C=O), 30.1
(Ar-CH2-), 34.3 (Ar-CH2CH2), 46.3 (-CH2- C=O), 47.2 (-C-CHO), 55.7
(-OCH3), 114.3 (Carommeta), 128.5 (Caromortho), 132.3 (Carom1), 149.8
(Carompara), 204.6 (-CHO) 206.7 (CH3- C=O); Microanalysis calcd/found: C:
72.55 72.76; H: 8.12 8.20.
