$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Wacker Oxidation of 3; General Procedure In a solution of substituted,
functionalized olefin 3a-h (1 equiv), in aq THF (THF/H2O, 1:9), were
suspended PdCl2 (0.1 equiv) and CuCl2 (0.1 equiv). This mixture was
stirred at r.t. under O2 (TLC control, 6-8 h). The mixture was diluted
with H2O and extracted with Et2O (3 × 20 mL). The combined Et2O layers
were washed with H2O, dried (Na2SO4), concentrated in vacuo and the crude
product was purified by column chromatography using 98:2 hexane-EtOAc as
eluent (Table 3). Compound 5a, yield 70%. Bp (°C)/Torr): 84-87/0.5. IR
(neat/Nujol) (cm-1) 3106, 2720, 1719, 1676, 1624, 1512, 1084, 1020, 824,
748, 699. 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ, J (Hz) 1.68 (s, 3 H, CCH3), 2.37 (s, 3 H,
ArCH3), 2.43 (s, 3 H, COCH3), 5.90 (s, 1 H, C=CHA E to acyl), 6.43 (s, 1
H, C=CHB Z to acyl), 7.10-7.50 (m, 4 H, ArH), 9.95 (s, 1 H, CHO). 13C NMR
(CDCl3), δ 20.6, 21.8, 26.1, 56.7, 127.1, 128.4, 129.2, 136.6, 137.1,
153.4, 198.4, 199.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM eliminative Wacker oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Eliminative Wacker oxidation: An efficient synthesis of α-alkyl vinyl
methyl ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kulkarni, Mukund G.; Davawala, Saryu I.; Doke, Aniruddha K.; Gaikwad,
Dayaneshwar D.; Doke, Ajit V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2005), (17), 2939-2945

