$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Bromoallylation of
Alkynes and Subsequent Wacker-Tsuji Oxidation (Table 1) To a solution of
allylbromide (173 μL, 2.00 mmol) in anhydrous DME (5.0 mL) cooled in an
ice-bath was added dibromo(bisbenzonitrile)palladium(II) (28.3 mg, 0.06
mmol). A solution of the alkyne (2.00 mmol) in anhydrous DME (5.0 mL) was
then added dropwise over ca. 30 min. The reaction mixture was stirred for
another 5.5 h at rt. H2O (5.0 mL) and copper (I) chloride (198 mg, 2.00
mmol) were subsequently added and the heterogenous reaction mixture
stirred under an atmosphere of oxygen (O2-filled balloon) for 24 h. The
mixture was subsequently diluted with H2O (5.0 mL) and enough 2N HCl was
added to form a homogenous solution. Et2O (50 mL) was then added and the
layers separated. The aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (3 × 10 mL)
and the combined organic extracts washed with sat. aqueous NaCl (30 ml.),
dried (MgSO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by flash silica gel chromatography (EtOAc/hexanes). Methyl
3-Bromo-2-(2-oxopropyl)acrylate (3a), 3a isolated as a clear, colorless
oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 6.69 (1H, t, J= 1.0 Hz), 3.73 (3H, s),
3.43 (2H, d, J= 1.0 Hz), 2.15 (3H, s); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 203.79,
165.15, 130.85,116.11,51.92,48.33,29.39; IR (film) ν 3070, 3003, 2953,
1720, 1617, 1436, 1357, 1214, 1165, 1122, 1029,988,960,855,818,769, 731,
667 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Multifunctional Palladium Catalysis. 2. Tandem Haloallylation Followed by
Wacker-Tsuji Oxidation or Sonogashira Cross-Coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Thadani, Avinash N.; Rawal, Viresh H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(24), 4321-4323

