$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The 4-pentenals 3a-h, PdCl2 (10 mol%), and
CuCl2 (10 mol%) were dissolved in aqueous DME (1:9) and stirred under an
oxygen atmosphere for 2-3 h. When the reaction was observed to be
complete, normal aqueous extractive work-up gave the ketoaldehydes 4a-h
in 71-84% yield. Compound 4f. viscous liquid, yield 73% IR [cm-1]
(neat/nujol): 2698.3, 1719.4, 1704.9; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ J (Hz): 0.9-1.05
(m, 6 H, 2 × CH3), 1.28-1.44 (m, 6 H, CH3CH2CH2-C, CH3CH2CH2CH2-),
1.52-1.63 (m, 4 H, 2 × -CH2-C-), 2.13 (s, 3 H, CH3-C=O), 2.67 (d, 1 H, J
= 17.3 Hz, O=C-CH2), 2.79 (d, 1 H, J = 17.3 Hz, O=CCH2), 9.61 (s, 1 H,
-CHO); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ : 13.9, 14.3 (CH3CH2-), 17.7 (CH3CH2CH2-C-),
23.1 (CH3CH2CH2CH2-), 26.2 (CH3CH2CH2CH2), 26.4 (CH3- C=O), 32.2
(CH3CH2CH2CH2- C), 33.4 (CH3CH2CH2-C), 44.9 (O=C-CH2), 47.8 (-C-CHO),
202.1 (-CHO), 205.4 (CH3- C=O); Microanalysis calcd/found: C: 72.68
72.83; H: 11.18 11.33.
