$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The 4-pentenals 3a-h, PdCl2 (10 mol%), and
CuCl2 (10 mol%) were dissolved in aqueous DME (1:9) and stirred under an
oxygen atmosphere for 2-3 h. When the reaction was observed to be
complete, normal aqueous extractive work-up gave the ketoaldehydes 4a-h
in 71-84% yield. Compound 4g. viscous liquid, yield 72% IR [cm-1]
(neat/nujol): 2701.2, 1717.3, 1705.8; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ J (Hz): 0.90-0.97
(t, 3 H, J= 7.1 Hz, -CH2CH3), 1.21 (s, 3 H, -CCH3), 1.54 (q, 2 H, J= 7.1
Hz, -CH2CH3), 2.11 (s, 3 H, CH3- C=O), 2.71 (d, 1 H, J = 17 Hz, O=C-CH2),
2.83 (d, 1 H, J = 17 Hz, O=C-CH2), 9.48 (s, 1 H, -CHO); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ
: 10.2 (CH3-CH2-), 16.1 (CH3- C-), 25.6 (CH3CH2-), 45.2 (O=C-CH2), 47.3
(-C-CHO), 202.4 (-CHO), 205.7 (CH3- C=O); Microanalysis calcd/found: C:
67.57 67.39; H: 9.92 9.84.
